---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { BRIEFS } from "../../lib/briefs";
import { linkClass, ext } from "../../lib/links";
import { newsArticleNode } from "../../lib/schema";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/base";

const brief = BRIEFS.find((b) => b.slug === "new-register")!;

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "Notes", path: "/brief" },
  { name: brief.title, path: brief.path },
];

const pageUrl = "https://fflintel.com/brief/new-register";
const hero = brief.image;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${brief.title} | FFL Intel`}
  description={brief.dek}
  path={brief.path}
  ogImagePath={hero}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  extraJsonLd={[
    newsArticleNode({
      url: pageUrl,
      headline: brief.title,
      description: brief.dek,
      datePublished: brief.date,
      dateModified: brief.date,
      image: `https://fflintel.com/${hero}`,
    }),
  ]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p
      class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-800 mb-3"
    >
      {brief.kicker}
    </p>
    <h1
      class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl text-balance mb-4"
    >
      {brief.title}
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-700 mb-6">{brief.dek}</p>
    <Byline dateLabel={brief.dateLabel} read={brief.read} />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-stone-200">
      <img
        src={withBase(hero)}
        alt={brief.imageAlt}
        width="1536"
        height="1024"
        class="w-full object-cover object-top max-h-80"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-[11px] text-stone-500">
        Gearfire Point of Sale, on the counter.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        A manufacturer reads last month’s same-store units and tries to write
        the next build. A retailer reads the same print and tries to decide
        what belongs on the wall. Both are working from completed demand: guns
        that already left the building. A down print gets quieter. It does not
        get more complete.
      </p>
      <p>
        The trade has been running on two series. The first is NICS. A Monday
        meeting still treats the FBI’s background-check count as if it were a
        cash register. Gearfire’s Kaleb Seymour said the same thing when
        RetailBI published its second-quarter 2026 report: the headline may be
        background checks, and the real market is what consumers actually buy,
        what they pay, and what remains on dealers’ shelves (Outdoor Wire, July
        2026). Permits, used guns, transfers, denials, and two guns on one
        check are why a NICS print is not a sales print.
      </p>
      <p>
        The second series is the RetailBI Firearm Sales Index: new guns, same
        stores, this year against last year, revised when more shops finish
        reporting. It is sell-through. It is useful. Gearfire's own{" "}
        <a
          href="https://gogearfire.com/solutions/retailbi/"
          class={linkClass}
          {...ext}>RetailBI page</a
        >, dated August 17, 2026, shows July down 0.8 percent at those same
        stores and the year to date down 4.3 percent. June printed up 2.0
        percent. Those are units, not dollars. They are not a press release.
        The last named monthly on Outdoor Wire is still March 2026, down 11.9
        percent (<a
          href="https://www.theoutdoorwire.com/releases/2026/04/retailbi-firearm-sales-index-reports-119-year-over-year-decline-in-march-2026/"
          class={linkClass}
          {...ext}>Outdoor Wire, April 13, 2026</a>). Gearfire's blog last
        wrote a monthly Index post for December 2025.
        In the second-quarter 2026 RetailBI report, new-firearm units declined
        while retail revenue rose as buyers shifted toward higher-priced
        products and dealers ran leaner inventory (Outdoor Wire, July 2026).
        Average selling price and mix can be up while units are down. If you
        only have the unit print, say so. If you only have the dollar print,
        say so. Neither print can see a shopper who typed a model and got
        nothing back.
      </p>
      <p>
        This week Gearfire launched Gearfire POS at $149 a month (<a
          href="https://www.theoutdoorwire.com/releases/2026/08/gearfire-launches-cloud-based-pos-built-for-specialty-outdoor-retailers/"
          class={linkClass}
          {...ext}>Outdoor Wire, August 18, 2026</a>). They first showed it at
        Kinsey’s in February. A better register will count the next sale more
        cleanly. It will not count the search that never became a sale.
      </p>
      <p>
        That empty search is the missing series. Someone opened a dealer site,
        searched for a gun, and did not find it. The shelf, the catalog, or the
        page had nothing. The Index never sees it, because empty never rings.
        Analytics records a session and stops. The shop has no name for it. The
        brand has no name for it. It is still demand. It showed up and left.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not have a monthly search-intent print to set beside minus 4.3,
        and we will not invent one. Sell-through and search are different jobs.
        How they sit together is on{" "}
        <a
          href="https://www.gunsearchengine.com/betsy-vs-retailbi"
          class={linkClass}
          {...ext}>Betsy vs RetailBI</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <p
        class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-800 mb-3"
      >
        Three numbers. Keep them apart.
      </p>
      <div
        class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-rule bg-white shadow-sm"
      >
        <table class="w-full min-w-[28rem] text-left text-sm">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule bg-stone-50">
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-sky-800"
              >
                Number
              </th>
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-500"
              >
                What it is
              </th>
              <th
                class="px-3 py-3 text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-stone-400"
              >
                What it is not
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule/80 align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">NICS</td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                FBI background-check counts
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                Gun sales
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule/80 align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">
                RetailBI Index
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                New guns sold at the same stores as last year
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                What people searched for
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="align-top">
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs font-medium text-ink">
                Search intent
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-700 leading-relaxed">
                What people searched for, including searches that came back
                empty
              </td>
              <td class="px-3 py-3 text-xs text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">
                A sales report
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-stone-700 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        <a href="https://fflintel.com" class={linkClass}>FFL Intel</a> is the
        journal of these three numbers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <LegalNote />
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-stone-500">
      Not affiliated with Gearfire or RetailBI. Marks of their owners. Published
      by Coriolis, LLC. Numbers by Betsy AI.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
